    {
      "evidence": "The spec says: \"When the CI version cannot be read... the step SHALL refuse explicitly naming both versions\". The docs (docs/engineering/agent-workflow.md) say \"an unreadable CI version ... [is] refused naming both versions\". scripts/check_ci_python.py:274 returns \"ci-python refused (local {local}, CI version unreadable): ...\", and test_unreadable_ci_version_is_refused_naming_the_local_version asserts exactly that text. No CI version exists to name in this case, so the contract wording is imprecise and the docs overstate it.",
      "id": "unreadable-ci-version-names-one-version",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The spec requires a refusal for an unreadable CI version to name both versions. The refusal can only name the local version. The docs repeat the claim."
    },
